# Architecture and coding

The app is the Next.js App Router in `app/`. Shared data access is `lib/supabase.ts`. Pages that use hooks or the browser Supabase client stay client components. Keep `app/layout.tsx` free of data fetching.

- Add a route by adding `app/<route>/page.tsx`. Do not invent `app/api` routes unless the task asks for a server boundary.
- Import the existing browser client. Do not construct a second Supabase client in a page.
- Preserve the Washington search, map, owner, and admin flows when editing shared types or queries.
- Query string links must be read by the destination page. City links use `/washington?city=&county=`. Map and demographics links use `?zip=`.
- Keep user-facing copy accurate. Do not say a feature is unavailable when the page implements it.
- Match the surrounding file's style. Do not add a styling framework or component library in a drive-by edit.

```tsx
// Good: one shared browser client
import { supabase } from "../../lib/supabase";

const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from("wa_dshs_listed_facilities")
  .select("id,canonical_name,license_number")
  .limit(20);
```
